+Added :func:`icalendar.parse <icalendar.cal.calendar.parse>`, which detects whether data is iCalendar, jCal, or xCal and parses it into calendars. It accepts :class:`bytes`, a :class:`~pathlib.Path`, or a binary file. Added the errors :class:`~icalendar.error.UnknownCalendarFormat`, :class:`~icalendar.error.NoCalendarsFound`, and :class:`~icalendar.error.CalendarInformationLost`. Added the how-to guide :doc:`/how-to/parse`. I used Claude Code as a learning aid to explain the codebase, review my code, and draft the tests and documentation, then reviewed and tested the result. @EyalHefer
